    - hardly could … contemplate the prospect of entering the safehold without asking that question,
      nor make headway in the philosophy without … an answer [in the context of the safehold]
\ to warrant these claims re (cQ) the question and (cA) its answer, the following:
\ to warrant (cQ), one of:
    | {[emphasis of] the fact|phenomenon of [impulsive] force and tension, of it being hard to resist
      both (i) reaching for the safehold and (ii) asking in regard to (i) the question}
        ' re warrant for (cQ): hell, it’s my [whole] *thesis* that I am morally obligated to ask that Q
          (which obligation entails|implies being compelled|impelled|forced to do so) and moreover
          that I do so in such a far-reaching context, a context in any case that demands a ground
            : note : notepad entry 2026-9-14a
        ' The *facts* of being forced|impelled i) to reach for the safehold and ii) to ask the Q
          in that regard — of being *hardly able to resist* reaching & asking — PLUS *my thesis*
          in regard to those facts: this may be the warrant that I seek for (cQ)
            : note : notepad entry 2026-9-14b
    | [the scale|scope of] the safehold makes remote and obscure the ultimate end,
      which in turn presses|urges the question, making it a must-ask as claimed
\ to warrant (cA):
    | working (in response to the impulse) to answer the question reveals that [the fact|phenomenon
